<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Backup rules.

    Only the app's own DataStore is backed up: the display name, the avatar choice, the theme
    and the location rules. Everything else is excluded by *omission* rather than by a list of
    excludes, which is why there are no <exclude> elements here — with a single <include>,
    anything not named is already left behind, and naming a domain that was never included is
    an error the resource compiler rejects.

    The Firebase anonymous session therefore does not travel with a restore. That is
    deliberate: it is the one thing that should be re-established on the device rather than
    transplanted, since it is what proves who the user is. The consequence is that a restored
    user has a new uid and is therefore no longer a member of the room whose id came back in
    the DataStore; the app reports that as "you are no longer in this room" rather than
    pretending the room is still reachable.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <include domain="file" path="datastore" />
</full-backup-content>
